    // Test 1: n=10, k=2 => combinations: 3+7, 5+5? but distinct so 3+7 only? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? Actually 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? Let's compute: primes: 2,3,5,7,11,... Pairs summing to 10: 3+7, 5+5 (not distinct), 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? 2+? Actually 2+8 no. So only 3+7.
